%% Describes declared application and Terraform behavior, not a live AWS trace.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / Browser

    box Public AWS delivery and API layer
        participant CF as CloudFront
        participant API as Regional API Gateway
    end
    box Private S3 origin
        participant S3 as S3 frontend bucket
    end
    box VPC private networking
        participant Lambda as Lambda get-members
        participant Endpoint as DynamoDB Gateway endpoint
    end
    box AWS regional data service
        participant DB as DynamoDB members table
    end

    Note over Client,DB: Static page and GET /members traffic<br/>No authentication or API key is configured for the member API

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over Client,S3: 1. Open the static website
        opt Browser initially uses HTTP
            Client->>CF: HTTP GET /
            CF-->>Client: Redirect to HTTPS
        end

        loop index.html and required JS, CSS, images, or documents
            Client->>CF: HTTPS GET / or /assets/{file}
            Note over Client,CF: AWS-managed default CloudFront certificate<br/>Default root object is index.html
            alt Valid cached static object
                CF-->>Client: 200 static content from edge cache
            else Cache miss or expired object
                CF->>S3: HTTPS GetObject with OAC SigV4 signature
                Note over CF,S3: Bucket policy permits CloudFront GetObject<br/>only for the configured distribution ARN
                Note over S3: Public access blocked, bucket-owner-enforced ownership<br/>AES256 encryption at rest, insecure non-service requests denied
                S3-->>CF: 200 static object
                Note over CF: Cache according to object headers and configured TTL limits<br/>index.html uses no-cache/no-store, other build assets use immutable caching
                CF-->>Client: 200 static content over HTTPS
            end
        end
        Client->>Client: Execute React app and display static page
    end

    rect rgb(235, 250, 240)
        Note over Client,DB: 2. User requests group members
        Client->>Client: Click the load-members button
        Client->>CF: HTTPS GET /members on the same website origin
        Note over CF: /members behavior selects the API origin<br/>CloudFront API caching is disabled, viewer Host is not forwarded
        CF->>API: HTTPS GET /{api_stage_name}/members<br/>TLS 1.2 to the regional API origin
        Note over API: Public GET method: authorization NONE, no API key<br/>Throttle rate 2 requests/second, burst 5, API caching disabled

        alt API request is throttled
            API-->>CF: 429 Too Many Requests
            CF-->>Client: 429 over HTTPS
            Client->>Client: Display error and offer retry
        else Request is accepted
            API->>Lambda: AWS_PROXY invocation through AWS Lambda service<br/>GET maps to a POST integration invocation
            Note over API,Lambda: Lambda permission is scoped to API ID, stage, GET, and /members<br/>Invocation is not inbound TCP traffic through the Lambda security group
            Note over Lambda,Endpoint: Function uses private subnet VPC networking<br/>No NAT or Internet Gateway is declared, no inbound SG rules<br/>SG egress allows TCP 443 only to the DynamoDB managed prefix list

            loop Scan pages until LastEvaluatedKey is absent
                Lambda->>Endpoint: HTTPS DynamoDB Scan signed with execution-role credentials<br/>Use ExclusiveStartKey after the first page
                Note over Endpoint: Gateway endpoint represents routing and policy enforcement<br/>It is not a proxy server or a separate application request
                Note over Endpoint,DB: Endpoint policy permits the members table and execution role<br/>Role IAM policy allows only dynamodb:Scan on that table
                Endpoint->>DB: Route the signed request through the AWS service network
                Note over DB: DynamoDB evaluates IAM authorization<br/>Server-side encryption and point-in-time recovery are enabled
                DB-->>Endpoint: Items and optional LastEvaluatedKey, or an error
                Endpoint-->>Lambda: Return the DynamoDB response
            end

            alt Scan and JSON serialization succeed
                Lambda->>Lambda: Add CloudFront /images/{studentId}.jpg URLs<br/>Convert Decimal values to JSON numbers
                Lambda-->>API: Proxy response: 200 and JSON member array
                API-->>CF: 200 application/json
                CF-->>Client: 200 JSON over HTTPS, no API edge cache
                Client->>Client: Render member names, IDs, and image URLs
            else Table access, scan, or serialization fails
                Lambda-->>API: Proxy response: 500 with generic error message<br/>Internal details remain in runtime logs
                API-->>CF: 500 application/json
                CF-->>Client: 500 over HTTPS
                Client->>Client: Display error and offer retry
            end
        end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 247, 230)
        Note over Client,S3: 3. Load member photos after a successful API response
        loop Each visible member photo
            Client->>CF: HTTPS GET /images/{studentId}.jpg
            alt Valid cached member photo
                CF-->>Client: 200 image from edge cache
            else Cache miss or expired photo
                CF->>S3: HTTPS GetObject with OAC SigV4 signature
                S3-->>CF: 200 image, Cache-Control public,max-age=3600
                CF-->>Client: 200 image over HTTPS
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Client,API: The execute-api URL is also publicly reachable over HTTPS<br/>CloudFront is not an authentication boundary, direct callers can bypass the CDN
    Note over Client,S3: Anonymous direct S3 reads are denied by the configured bucket controls<br/>IAM permissions still govern authorized administrative access